  "answer": "This request, Mouse Without Borders support for Android phones, has been reported before and is tracked in PowerToys#26296 (Mouse Without Borders for Android and other OSs). Similar tickets (#34667, #29364, #33575) were closed as duplicates of it, so add your +1 and any extra context there instead of in a new ticket. No Android support exists in PowerToys today. Until it does, the ticket's comments suggest scrcpy (https://github.com/Genymobile/scrcpy) to view and control an Android phone from your PC. It mirrors the screen rather than letting your cursor move between devices, so it is not the same as Mouse Without Borders. Barrier and Synergy are other options, but they cover Linux and macOS and do not add Android support."
